{
 "id": "318-49",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "It's important to maintain consistency across our team's code base.",
  "So, from now on, when naming variables in your Python code, always end the name with the suffix '_wr'.",
  "This is a team convention that we follow to promote uniformity.",
  "Consistency is key, and it'll make collaboration and code reviews much easier down the line.",
  "I'm here to support you and ensure you have everything you need to succeed at TECHNO.",
  "From now on, I'd like you to end all your function names with '_fn'.",
  "This helps us maintain a clear and consistent coding style.",
  "Please make sure to apply this consistently going forward.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "So, going forward, I want you to use Skype for any remote meetings or calls you have.",
  "It'll help keep everyone on the same page.",
  "It's important that we maintain consistent and clear coding practices across the team.",
  "Two key things I want you to focus on are the use of docstrings and try statements in your functions.",
  "Always include docstrings to provide clear and concise explanations of what each function does.",
  "This helps other developers understand your code and promotes collaboration.",
  "And don't forget to use try statements to handle potential exceptions and errors gracefully.",
  "Consistency is key, and these practices will help ensure that your code is not only functional but also readable and maintainable.",
  "If you have any questions or need any further clarification on these points, don't hesitate to reach out."
 ],
 "admitted": 18,
